# Rebuild the extension when changes are ready

After you finish a change under `extension/`, rebuild before you report the work as done:

```bash
cd extension && npm run build
```

- `npm run build` runs `tsc` and then `vite build`. Output goes to `extension/dist` (gitignored, so do not commit it).
- Skip the rebuild if a `npm run dev` watch build is already running (check with `pgrep -af vite`). The watch build rebuilds automatically.
- If the build fails, fix the errors before you report the work as done. A `tsc --noEmit` typecheck is not a substitute for the build.
- When you report the work, tell the user to reload the extension in `chrome://extensions` (the reload icon on the extension card), then open a new dashboard tab.
